# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Range42 Deployer UI — environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and edit the values for your machine.
# Only variables prefixed `VITE_` are exposed to the browser bundle.

# Host port for the web interface (Docker container / compose).
UI_PORT=3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev server (vite dev only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite dev server port. Playwright's `playwright.config.ts` reads this too.
# VITE_DEV_PORT=3000

# Host to advertise to the HMR client when the dev server is reachable from
# another machine (e.g. a Proxmox jump host). Leave unset for localhost — Vite
# will infer the HMR URL from the page origin.
# VITE_HMR_HOST=192.168.42.123

# Backend API base URL. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000 when unset.
# In dev, the UI issues relative `/v1/*` requests — Vite proxies them to this
# URL. In production (Docker + nginx), nginx proxies `/v1/*` upstream and this
# variable is ignored.
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git provider tokens (reference only — not read from env at runtime)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The UI reads real provider tokens from the Sources store (localStorage key
# `range42_git_sources`), populated via the `/sources` page. The entries below
# are documentation for which scopes each provider requires when minting
# Personal Access Tokens. Do not paste live secrets here and do not commit
# `.env.local` to version control.

# GitHub — classic PAT or fine-grained token
#   Required scopes: `repo` (full control of private repositories — read +
#     write contents, pull requests, forks, branches).
#   Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/managing-your-personal-access-tokens
# VITE_EXAMPLE_GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# GitLab — Personal Access Token (self-hosted or gitlab.com)
#   Required scopes: `api` (full read + write) OR the narrower pair
#     `read_repository` + `write_repository` if full API access is not needed.
#   Docs: https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/profile/personal_access_tokens.html
# VITE_EXAMPLE_GITLAB_TOKEN=glpat-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Gitea — access token (self-hosted)
#   Required scopes: `repo` (read + write to repositories, branches, contents,
#     pull requests). Gitea 1.20+ uses the same coarse scope model as GitHub.
#   Docs: https://docs.gitea.io/en-us/api-usage/#authentication
# VITE_EXAMPLE_GITEA_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
